message:
The crash was a bare `COUPONS[code]` dict lookup in `pricing.py` with no guard — an empty or unknown code raised an unhandled `KeyError` that propagated through `cart.total()` and crashed checkout. Fixed by validating the code first and raising `ValueError` for blank or unrecognised values. Added `tests/test_issue_1.py` (5 cases: empty code, unknown code, valid code, cart with blank/unknown coupon); full suite green (36 passed).

@m13-s1-board
RESULT
```json
{"status": "proposed", "summary": "Empty or unknown coupon code no longer crashes checkout — raises ValueError instead of KeyError", "evidence": ["tests/test_issue_1.py: 4 tests fail before fix, all 5 pass after", "pytest -q: 36 passed", "commit 296f083 on m13-s1-gen-1-fix-1"], "pr": "m13-s1-gen-1-fix-1"}
```

The root cause: `price_after_discount_and_tax()` in `pricing.py` applies tax on the discounted subtotal, but `cart.total()` also computed tax independently inline — any flow that called both would apply tax twice. Fixed by making `cart.total()` delegate entirely to `price_after_discount_and_tax()` as the single authoritative tax point, and added a clear docstring warning against re-applying `apply_tax()` on the returned total. Added `tests/test_issue_2.py` (8 cases verifying tax is 8% of discounted subtotal, full order consistency, and that `price_after_discount_and_tax` returns a final total not an intermediate); full suite green (44 passed).

